 Feature exerciser — lists              
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 
                                        
 Every list shape the parser can        
 produce, so bullets, numbering,        
 indentation and the tight/loose        
 distinction can all be compared on one 
 screen.                                
                                        
 Unordered, tight                       
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 · one                                  
 · two                                  
 · three                                
                                        
 Unordered, loose                       
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 · one                                  
                                        
 · two                                  
                                        
 · three                                
                                        
 Marker spellings                       
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 · dash                                 
                                        
 · star                                 
                                        
 · plus                                 
                                        
 Ordered, tight                         
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 1. first                               
 2. second                              
 3. third                               
                                        
 Ordered, loose, starting elsewhere     
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 7. seventh                             
                                        
 8. eighth                              
                                        
 9. ninth                               
                                        
 Ordered with a wide number             
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
  98. ninety-eight                      
                                        
  99. ninety-nine                       
                                        
 100. one hundred, where the marker     
      grows a column and the text must  
      stay aligned                      
                                        
 101. one hundred and one               
                                        
 Ordered with the other delimiter       
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 1. parenthesis form                    
 2. second                              
                                        
 Items that wrap                        
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 · A list item long enough that it must 
   wrap even at one hundred and twenty  
   columns, so the continuation lines   
   can be checked for hanging           
   indentation against the bullet that  
   introduced them.                     
                                        
 · A short one after it.                
                                        
 1. An ordered item that also wraps, so 
    the hanging indent under a numeric  
    marker can be compared with the one 
    under a bullet — they should agree. 
                                        
 2. Short.                              
                                        
 Nested five deep                       
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 · level one                            
   – level two                          
     ▪ level three                      
       ▫ level four                     
         · level five, and this one     
           wraps as well so the deepest 
           indentation can be seen      
           against a forty column pane  
                                        
       ▫ back to four                   
                                        
   – back to two                        
                                        
 · back to one                          
                                        
 Ordered inside unordered inside        
 ordered                                
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 1. ordered one                         
    – unordered inside                  
      1. ordered inside that            
      2. and a sibling                  
                                        
    – another unordered                 
                                        
 2. ordered two                         
                                        
 Task lists                             
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 ☑ a finished task                      
                                        
 ☐ an unfinished task                   
                                        
 ☑ a finished task with a capital       
   marker                               
                                        
 ☐ a task long enough to wrap so the    
   checkbox column can be checked       
   against the continuation indent      
                                        
 · a plain item mixed into a task list  
   ☐ a nested unfinished task           
   ☑ a nested finished task             
                                        
 Ordered task list                      
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 ☑  a finished numbered task            
 ☐  an unfinished numbered task         
                                        
 Items containing other blocks          
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 · An item with a paragraph.            
                                        
   And a second paragraph inside the    
   same item.                           
                                        
 · An item with a quote:                
                                        
   ▌ quoted inside a list item          
                                        
 · An item with code:                   
                                        
   ╭ rust ────────────────────────────╮ 
   │ fn in_a_list() {}                │ 
   ╰──────────────────────────────────╯ 
                                        
 · An item with a table:                
                                        
   ╭───┬───╮                            
   │ a │ b │                            
   ├───┼───┤                            
   │ 1 │ 2 │                            
   ╰───┴───╯                            
                                        
 · An item with a nested diagram, which 
   the pager deliberately does not      
   widen:                               
                                        
   ┌───────────┐   ┌─────────────────┐  
   │ In a list ├──▶│ Still in a list │  
   └───────────┘   └─────────────────┘  
                                        
 Degenerate                             
 ────────────────────────────────────── 
                                        
 ·                                      
 · an empty item precedes this one      
                                        
 1.                                     
                                        
 2. an empty ordered item precedes this 
    one
